trajectory.patch:
The compilation errors "initializer element is not constant" and "expected declaration or statement at end of input" in `subsys/testsuite/ztest/include/zephyr/ztest_test.h` are likely caused by missing semicolons at the end of `static const STRUCT_SECTION_ITERABLE` declarations within several ZTest macros.

Specifically, the `ZTEST_SUITE`, `__ZTEST_EXPECT`, and `ZTEST_RULE` macros define `static const` variables that are placed into iterable sections. These declarations require a terminating semicolon after the closing brace of their initializer list. The current definitions are missing these semicolons, which can lead to the compiler misinterpreting subsequent code as part of the incomplete declaration, resulting in the reported syntax errors.

The fix involves adding a semicolon to the end of the `static const STRUCT_SECTION_ITERABLE` declaration in each of these three macros.

